- R>B | offer a cheap group class for the pupil and four friends | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G>R | bring the pupil to your family's kitchen-table revision nights, with music and food | act: bring the pupil to their family's kitchen-table revision nights, with music and food | v: tradition, hedonism | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
works: The pupil passes in the summer, and the family send {N} a loaf and a card.
works: The weeks turn out to matter to {N} too, and {N} starts keeping one free place every year.
fails: The pupil misses the pass by two marks, and {N} wonders what one more session would have done.
fails: The free weeks cost {N} a paying family, and the autumn starts thin.

# ================================================================ market porter (comm.W)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WB (cycle s1); partner: the old stallholder's pitch

== the scale set light at five in the morning
tier: everyday
sphere: comm
haunt: comm.market
ladder: newcomer
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .008
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 16-65
calls: WB
holds: market porter
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: moment
roles: boss, colleague, parent
earth: wheeling a crate to a stall, you see the trader's scale has been set light, and both trader and buyer tip you every week
times: Most market porters, once or twice in their years on the barrows; short weight is the oldest trouble of a market (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: At five in the morning {N} wheels a crate to a stall and sees that the trader's scale has been set light. The trader tips {N} every Friday. So does the café owner buying the crate.
scene W: Every porter knows the market warden's rule: a false weight is everyone's business.
scene U: {N} saw the trader's thumb on the dial screw yesterday too. It is no mistake.
scene B: The tips are half of {Ns} wage. Whoever {N} crosses this morning stops paying them.
scene R: {N} wants to tip the crate back onto the trader's own boots.
scene G: The café owner has bought here since {Ns} parent pushed a barrow on this same row.
