earth: near closing a young customer is too drunk to stand, their friends have gone, and the rule is to put them outside
times: Most door staff, many times a year; a customer left alone and too drunk to get home is the commonest worry of the night's last hour (estimate)
gap: 0-0.5
scene: Near closing, a young customer is too drunk to stand, and the friends who came with them have gone. The night manager's rule is simple: anyone that drunk goes outside the door.
scene W: The rule keeps the room safe for everyone. It was never meant to leave someone alone on a cold pavement.
scene U: {N} has seen nights like this go wrong after the door, not before it. The taxi rank is empty at this hour.
scene B: {N} is paid to keep the door, not to mind the customers. The manager watches who keeps to the rule.
scene R: {N} wants to get this one home, rule or no rule.
scene G: {N} grew up four streets away, and this could be a neighbour's child.
- W | sit them by the cloakroom with water until someone sober can take them | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | ask which way they live, and work out the safest way to get them there | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | put them outside as the rule says, and get back to the door | v: conformity, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | walk them to the taxi rank yourself, and wait until a car comes | act: walk them to the taxi rank and wait until a car comes | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | ring round the regulars until someone knows the family | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>R | log it by the book, then go off shift and walk them home | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>G | work out from their talk which friends they came with, and find them nearby | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>W | tell the manager the licence is at risk if they are left outside | v: power, security | lever: voice | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>U | stay out on the pavement with them and keep them talking until help comes | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>B | call your cousin who drives a taxi, and settle the fare between you | act: call their cousin who drives a taxi, and settle the fare between them | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: The customer gets home safe, and a week later comes back sober to thank the door staff.
works: The manager sees how it was handled and gives {N} the Saturday shifts.
fails: The manager is furious about the time it took, and {N} loses a shift that week.
fails: The friends turn up at last, angry and blaming the door, and the night ends in shouting.

